Z||000000||WaltR||09-21-2001||01:30 PM||||Does anyone know the diameter of the round plugs in the 87-88 headlight motors? I do not have one handy to check this.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||09-21-2001||01:48 PM||||Approx 12mm||||reg||1
Z||000002||WaltR||09-21-2001||02:36 PM||||Thanks. Thats what I needed.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-21-2001||07:45 PM||||2 rebuild kits is $10, including shipping, from Rodney. Unlike some other sources they are exact fit. I used them to do mine last year.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||My7Fieros||09-21-2001||09:15 PM||||Glue sticks work great. I rebuilt the headlight motors in my 88 two years ago....worked great ever since.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000005||SLYGUY||09-21-2001||11:11 PM||||My left headlight would dance around and not make it all the way up. I bought a couple of rebuild kits from Rodney. <P>Cylinder like plastic plugs. Look like the ear plugs you put in your ears. <P>I took apart the headlight assembly and actuator. Followed the directions and there was nothing left of the original "bushings". Only a fine white powder. <BR>Put the new bushings in like the directions said, put it all back together and works great now. Easy fix.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000006||Spektrum-87GT||09-21-2001||11:47 PM||||how long does it usually take for him to ship? just sent out the money, just wondering when i should be expecting them, i want to drive at night dangit!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||SLYGUY||09-22-2001||12:21 AM||||Having to pull the headlights while people watch you makes this take FOREVER..<P>Don't worry. I don't remember how long it took, but it wasn't long. Depends on where you are, and if the recent tragedy in NY will slow down delivery.<P>One particular about the directions:<P>In the directions it disassemble the gear, rod and cap assembly. When you lift it up and see all of the white powder in there that used to be your bushings just blow it out yourself or with some kind of air gun. Make sure there are no deposits and put your new bushings in. Slide the gear, rod, and bushings carefully together making sure that the bushings align like they should and not crimp. <P>Reassemble and all should be well. You'll love it when you see both the headlights go up from INSIDE the car at night!!'<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000008||Spektrum-87GT||09-22-2001||07:13 PM||||just got the rebuild kit today, woohoo! pretty quick shipping, its funny how something that small can cause the headlights to go wacko, anyway, i'll probably be ordering from rodney again!||||reg||1
